## Detailed description of every kind that fires

### 0 — PistonQueued
**Where:** `checkForMove` (`simulator.cpp:969-997`), on every extend/retract transition a piston's
`shouldPistonBeExtended` computes.
**Fields:** `blockKey`/`actorKey` = piston's live position (not stable key — a moving piston hasn't
relocated between queue and execute). `direction`, `SEF_EXTEND`. **SDL10:** `SEF_QUEUE_DEDUPED` set
when `addBlockEvent` silently discarded this as a duplicate of an already-pending entry — measured
23,334/78,104 (30%) on `1-wide with rails`, so this is not a rare case.
**Meaning:** "the simulator decided this piston should extend/retract" — intent, not outcome. Two
thirds of these never produce a `PistonMoveExecuted` (rejected later in `fireBlockEvent`/
`pistonEventReceived`, or discarded on arrival per `SEF_QUEUE_DEDUPED`).

### 1 — PistonMoveExecuted
**Where:** `doPistonMove` (`simulator.cpp:1719-1803`), both the failure branch (`:1746`) and the
success branch (`:1789`).
**Fields:** `direction`, `SEF_EXTEND`, `SEF_SUCCESS` (clear = blocked), `failureReason` (one of the
8 `SimFailureReason` values) when blocked, `attemptedAmount`/`actualAmount` = push group size,
`pushGroupId`, `scheduledTick/Subtick` = when it was queued (via `takeQueued`).
**Meaning:** the piston's own action record — moved, or tried and failed and why. This is also the
only place `PushGroupRecord` gets written (`:1773`, `:1806`), which carries full group membership.

### 2 — BlockPushed
**Where:** three sites, all inside `doPistonMove`: the main per-block loop (`:1872`, one per
carried block), the extending head (`simulator.cpp:1919-1941`, added this session), and the
retracting head/arm (`simulator.cpp` inside `pistonEventReceived`'s retract branch, added this
session).
**Fields:** `actorKey` = piston, `targetKey` = destination cell, `direction`, `SEF_EXTEND`,
`pushGroupId`. **SDL10:** `reserved2` = the full raw state word that will land when the flight
ends (the whole reason for this session's work — see "the resume-completeness fix" below).
`SEF_SELF_ARM` marks the head/retract-arm variant (subject is the piston itself, not a
relocating block).
**Meaning:** "a flight began." Every entry ever added to `World::movingBuckets` now has exactly one
of these starting it.

### 3 — ObserverFired
**Where:** `observerUpdateTick` (`simulator.cpp:745-793` region, both the powered-on and
powered-off scheduled-update paths).
**Fields:** `SEC_SCHEDULED`/`SEC_FACING_CHANGED`/`SEC_OBSERVER_MOVED` cause in flags bits 2-3,
`SEF_OBSERVER_ON` (set = the ON pulse, clear = the OFF transition 2 ticks later — same function,
re-invoked via its own scheduled tick). `from`/`to` = the observer's live position (populated
SDL8).
**Meaning:** the observer's own pulse, cause included. Only present in 6/9 fixtures — the 3 without
it use only redstone-block power, no observers.

### 4 — ObserverActivated
**Where:** `logObserverActivations` (`simulator.cpp:912-945`), a fan-out scan of the block in front
of the observer plus that block's 4 side neighbours.
**Fields:** `targetKey` = the piston/observer reached, `SEF_TARGET_PISTON` (else observer),
`SEF_OBSERVER_ON`, `from` = observer, `to` = target (both live positions, SDL8).
**Meaning:** "this pulse reached that specific piston/observer." Measured 1.37 targets per pulse —
this is the expanded, per-target form of kind 3.

### 5 — RedstoneBlockAppeared / 6 — RedstoneBlockRemoved
**Where:** `setBlockState`'s block-type-change hook (`simulator.cpp:2073-2107`), whenever a redstone
block (id) appears/disappears at a cell, whether by placement, destruction, or being carried by a
push.
**Fields:** `blockKey`/`actorKey` = stable id. **SDL10:** `from`==`to`== the live cell (previously
100% `(0,0,0)`, fixed this session).
**Meaning:** existence, not power — appearing/disappearing at a position, not "now providing power."
Each one triggers `logRedstonePistonScan` immediately after (kinds 7/8).

### 7 — RedstoneActivatedPiston / 8 — RedstoneDeactivatedPiston
**Where:** `logRedstonePistonScan` (`simulator.cpp:950-981`), called from 5/6 above and also
directly from the initial-load piston scan (`:2674`).
**Fields:** `targetKey` = piston, `SEF_TARGET_PISTON`. **SDL10:** `from` = redstone block,
`to` = piston (previously 100% `(0,0,0)`, fixed this session).
**Meaning:** the per-neighbour-piston consequence of 5/6 — "this specific piston is now
powered/unpowered by that redstone block." Same fan-out relationship to 5/6 that 4 has to 3.

### 12 — BlockDestroyed
**Where:** `logBlockDestroyed` (`simulator.cpp:467-489`), called from 5 distinct sites covering all
5 `SED_*` causes: rail losing support, push-destroy (`PushReaction::Destroy` blocks popped by a
push), orphaned piston head, orphaned extended base, head removed on retract.
**Fields:** `reserved1` = `SED_*` cause byte.
**Meaning:** "this block stopped existing, and here is which rule did it" — the cascading-deletion
cases (orphan head/base) are only knowable through this record; nothing else states them.

### 15 — PistonNeighborNotified
**Where:** the generic `notifyNeighbors`/`neighborChangedImpl` path (`simulator.cpp` — the catch-all
6-neighbour poke every block placement performs), whenever the notified block is a piston with no
more specific kind (4/7/8/2-self) already covering the cause.
**Fields:** `actorKey` = stableKey of the position that changed, `reserved0` = the raw block id that
was there *before* the change.
**Meaning:** "this piston was poked because something changed next to it, for a reason none of the
more specific kinds capture" — the largest single kind by volume (16.45%). Re-verified this session:
only 73-91% of these coincide with a same-tick `BlockStateChanged` at the notifying position; the
rest are explicit `neighborChanged`/`notifyNeighbors` calls with no accompanying write. **Not
redundant** — this was checked twice now and both times the "should be derivable" prediction failed
measurement.

### 16 — ScheduledTickDropped
**Where:** `scheduleUpdate` (`simulator.cpp:647-680` region), when an identical `(pos, blockId)`
scheduled tick is already pending.
**Fields:** `reserved0` = the blockIdValue attempted.
**Meaning:** the "attempt failed, nothing changed" counterpart to kind 20. Only appears in 1/9
fixtures (rail-bearing/lamp machines).

### 17 — BlockPoweredChanged
**Where:** `logPoweredChanged` (`simulator.cpp:318-343`), shared by rail (golden/activator),
fence gate, trapdoor, and redstone lamp toggling their own powered/open/lit bit.
**Fields:** `reserved0` = raw block id (disambiguates which of the four), `SEF_POWERED_ON`.
**Meaning:** a block's own state flag flipping, as opposed to it moving or being destroyed. Rare
(0.07%) — only 1 fixture in the corpus exercises this path.

### 18 — BlockSettled
**Where:** `logMovingBlockEnded` (`simulator.cpp:344-378`), called from `settleMovingBlock` on the
normal T+2 completion path and from `clearMovingAt` on early-cancel paths.
**Fields:** `pushGroupId` (pairs back to the `BlockPushed` that started this flight), `reserved0` =
raw carried block id, `reserved1` = `SEM_*` cause (which of 5 different paths ended the flight —
normal, head-cancelled, sticky-pullback, cell-overwritten, not-placeholder), `scheduledTick/Subtick`
= flight start, `executedTick/Subtick` = actual landing (duration is NOT a constant 2 — 2,040
one-tick arrivals measured on `1-wide with rails`).
**Meaning:** "a flight ended, successfully." Pairs 1:1 with a `BlockPushed` since this session's fix
(previously 15,962+ unpaired).

### 20 — ScheduledTickCreated
**Where:** `logScheduledTickCreated` (`simulator.cpp:407-434` region), the success counterpart to
kind 16, called from `scheduleUpdate` whenever a new tick is actually queued.
**Fields:** `reserved0` = blockIdValue scheduled, `attemptedAmount` = delay in ticks, `reserved2` =
the `ScheduledTick.order` tiebreak (needed to reproduce within-tick execution order of scheduled
updates — this value appears nowhere else), `executedTick` = when queued, `scheduledTick` = when
due.
**Meaning:** live queue state insertion. Consumption (the tick actually firing, or being silently
skipped because the block changed underneath) is not logged separately but is fully derivable —
everything with `time <= now` leaves the queue deterministically.

### 21 — RailShapeChanged
**Where:** `logRailShapeChanged` (`simulator.cpp:385-406` region), called from `Rail.place`/
`railConnectTo` whenever a rail rewrites its own or a neighbour's shape metadata.
**Fields:** `reserved0` = raw block id, `reserved2` = the full new raw state word.
**Meaning:** the one state change that genuinely cannot be inferred — it runs vanilla's full shape
selection including the powered-hint corner tiebreak against the live neighbourhood. Rare in this
corpus (78 events, 1 fixture) only because few fixtures use rails, not because it's rare per rail
machine.

### 22 — BlockStateChanged
**Where:** inside `setBlockState` itself (`simulator.cpp`), for EVERY world write that actually
changes something, regardless of which rule caused it. The choke-point backstop added in SDL9.
**Fields:** `targetKey` = old raw state word, `reserved2` = new raw state word, `attemptedAmount` =
the caller's `flags` argument (decides the neighbour/observer cascade that follows).
**Meaning:** the ground truth of world state. This is the largest kind by far (36.34%) and is what
makes the log replay-complete by construction — no rule needs re-implementing and none can silently
escape the log, because this fires regardless of *why* the write happened.

