## Recommended next step, if pursued

Only one item rises to "worth doing": **the kind-22 compact section** — `(globalSeq, position,
newState, flags)`, NOT `(globalSeq, newState, flags)` (see the correction above: position cannot be
dropped, 20.8–34.5% of writes collide on `(tick, position)`). It's still the single largest lever —
roughly 80–84% off this kind, ~30% of total log volume — and every other candidate above is either
already justified to keep (15, 0, 18, 21) or a small, judgement-call trim (4/7/8, 5/6) that trades
supervision richness for a few percent of file size.

