## Update: tick-chunked data layer implemented

Following this catalogue, a per-tick recurrent training data layer was built (the "auto-recursion
over a full tick" design) to make training on these logs tractable — full-run attention was
infeasible (`1-wide with rails` is 1,014,080 events) and the existing whole-board model couldn't
even encode 21 of 55 fixtures (dense `[5,N,N]` relation tensor, up to 71 GB on the largest
fixture). New/changed:

- `transformer gym/transformer_gym/encode.py` — relations are now a sparse edge list
  (`rel_edges: [3,E]`), not a dense matrix; `build_graph()` factored out as the shared static-node
  builder. All 55 fixtures now encode (was 34/55).
- `transformer gym/transformer_gym/model.py` — edge-restricted attention replacing dense
  relation-biased global attention. A real semantic change (a node can no longer attend anywhere),
  not just a memory optimization — needs a before/after accuracy check once trainable (not run in
  this environment: no PyTorch installed here, syntax-checked only).
- `util tools/simlog_ticks.py` — chronological, tick-grouped event reader (k-way merge across the
  format's block-major on-disk layout).
- `transformer gym/transformer_gym/state.py` — `SimState`/`apply_tick`: the per-tick "sufficient
  statistic" (board + in-flight blocks + both queues) an autoregressive model would condition on.
  Verified against ground truth at **every tick boundary** of all 9 fixtures (4,106 tick checks,
  100% match) by `util tools/check_state_builder.py`.
- `transformer gym/transformer_gym/dataset.py` — sparse-edge `collate()`; new `TickChunkDataset`.

One design assumption was caught and corrected by that verification: `pending_block_events` was
assumed to always empty out within the tick it was queued (checkForMove and
sendQueuedBlockEvents both run inside one tickWorld() call). Measured false — `movableRCA` ends
with 5 entries that were queued once and never resolved, because a queued move can be silently
rejected with no event logged (the pre-existing "block-event rejection is unlogged" gap). The field
is documented as a conservative over-approximation now, not an exact queue state.

Model/training code (causal event-sequence model, teacher-forcing curriculum, rollout eval) was
deliberately left unbuilt — data layer only, confirmed scope.
